win32u: Reuse an existing family when loading the font cache.

Each process loads the host's fonts before it reads Wine's font cache. A cache family with the name
of a family the process already has (Creative Cloud's Adobe Fonts sync adds fonts such as Open Sans
with AddFontResource and removes them again, which leaves empty family keys) was created a second
time: it could not enter the family name tree, got no faces, and releasing it removed a node that
wasn't in the tree. The corrupted tree crashed every process started afterwards in user32
initialization (no GDI stock objects, windows can't be created): conhost storms, and the VC++
installer that CC 6.11's self-update runs failed with 0x80070005 loading its loc file. Look the
family up on every load, not only on a refresh (patch 0043).

--- a/dlls/win32u/font.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/font.c
@@ -1362,10 +1362,12 @@
         if (!query_reg_value( hkey_family, NULL, info, sizeof(buffer) ))
             second_name[0] = 0;
 
-        /* On a refresh the family may already exist (this process added the face itself):
-         * a second family of that name would not enter the name tree, and releasing it
-         * would remove the existing family's tree entry. */
-        if (newer_than && (family = find_family_from_name( family_name ))) family->refcount++;
+        /* The family may already exist: this process added the face itself (refresh), or it
+         * loaded a host font of that name before reading the cache (fonts that another process
+         * added and removed again leave empty family keys behind, such as Adobe Fonts synced by
+         * Creative Cloud). A second family of that name would not enter the name tree, and
+         * releasing it would remove a node that isn't there and corrupt the tree. */
+        if ((family = find_family_from_name( family_name ))) family->refcount++;
         else family = create_family( family_name, second_name );
 
         load_face_from_cache( hkey_family, family, buffer, sizeof(buffer), TRUE, newer_than != NULL );
